# Rule: Simula paper alignment (repo-local)

Applies to this repository only.

## Required references (for medium/large tasks)
Before implementation/planning decisions, consult:
- `docs/research_paper.pdf`
- `docs/adr/0001-research-first-scope.md`
- `docs/adr/0002-control-axes-as-first-class.md`
- `docs/adr/0003-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds.md`
- `contexts/core/CONTEXT.md`
- `contexts/eval/CONTEXT.md`

## Required workflow
- Medium/large tasks: run `/grill-with-docs` first.
- Implementation tasks: prefer `/tdd`.
- Failures/regressions: run `/diagnose` before proposing fixes.

## Hard constraints
- Do NOT change thresholds/metric formulas/ablation protocol without explicit justification grounded in `docs/research_paper.pdf` and ADR impact notes.
- Preserve baseline/ablation comparability unless explicitly approved.
- Do reproducibility checks before interpreting weak/failed metrics.

## Required response section (substantial work)
Include `Paper Alignment Check` with:
1) Traceability/Auditability
2) Protocol/Comparability
3) Control-axis impact (coverage/complexity/quality)
4) Deviations (or `none`)

## Escalation
If alignment is ambiguous, ask for HITL clarification instead of assuming.
